# ============================================================================
# secrets.map.example -> copy to secrets.map
# Maps "an env name in your app" to "a secret that already exists in the Secret
# Manager of your team":
#   ENV_NAME=secret-name:latest
# - You can use only secrets that start with <prefix>- and that you have permission
#   to read (see ./kit.sh secrets).
# - These are reference names only. Never write a real secret value here.
# - For your own API keys, use the slots <prefix>-app-secret-1..5 that the portal
#   created for you:
#     ./kit.sh secrets add 1                         (hidden input)
#     ./kit.sh secrets map OPENAI_API_KEY 1          (adds the line below for you)
#   You cannot read the value back from the web. To change a value, add a new version.
# - You cannot create a new secret outside the slots -> ask the TA.
# - The DATABASE_URL that the portal attached to the service/job already works, so
#   you do not need to list it here (you may list it to make it clear, but you
#   cannot read its value directly).
# ============================================================================
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=grp01-admin-password:latest
# DEMO_USER_PASSWORD=grp01-demo-password:latest
# DATABASE_URL=grp01-database-url:latest
# OPENAI_API_KEY=grp01-app-secret-1:latest
